 ],
 "notes": "Faces +Z, origin between the feet. Idle stance (hunched): 1.23 m to the top of the back/fans; bounds.radius 0.59 m = body core (pelvis/spine/legs) for collision; head-to-tail extent (bounds.extent_radius) 0.93 m and blade tips (bounds.blade_reach) 0.97 m from the origin (culling / melee range). Units metres. All clips 60 fps, root bone static in every clip (all motion is on pelvis and below). run: in place, ground speed 8.0 m/s (feet planted at exactly 8 m/s during contact), 36-frame loop (0.600 s), footstep_l at 0.000 s, footstep_r at 0.300 s, both feet off the ground between contacts. idle: 3 s loop with stepped head darts and weight shifts; events flick (right blade) and scrape (claw); its frame 0 is the reference pose every one-shot starts and ends on (spawn ends on it, deaths start on it). leap: fully in place incl. height - the clip only crouches/extends/tucks; between 'launch' (0.330 s) and 'land' (0.700 s) the game should move the root along its ballistic arc so the root is back on the ground at 'land'; 'impact' (0.745 s) = both blades hit the ground in front. attack_a: right-blade arcing slash with a lunge step, telegraph 0.190 s, impact 0.267 s (the tip passes a chest-high point ~1.3 m in front), body returns to its spot (no root motion). attack_b: two-blade horizontal scissor from a wide overhead spread, telegraph 0.240 s, impact 0.365 s. hit: additive flinch authored as deltas on idle frame 0 - use THREE.AnimationUtils.makeClipAdditive(hit, 0); only spine/neck/head/arm/blade/fan/dorsal tracks move, pelvis/legs/tail tracks are constant (zero delta), so it layers over run or idle. stagger: vulnerable window 0.10-0.95 s (events vulnerable_start/_end), stumbles back and steps back to its spot (ends where it started). death_a: forward collapse, pelvis ends 1.15 m ahead of the origin lying prone; death_b: blown back, lands on its back and rolls onto its side, pelvis ends 1.62 m behind the origin. Deaths do not move the root; keep the corpse at the death position. Glow: every clip that changes heat carries a meta 'glow' curve per material (core_glow, blade_glow; k multiplies the authored emissive) - these are authoritative (spawn ignition, attack flares, stagger flicker, death gutter to 0). The events gutter_start/gutter_end (deaths) and ignite_start/ignite_full (spawn) remain as FX cues. Materials: ceramic (plates), sinew (under-structure), core_glow (core, seams, inner tubes, head slit) and blade_glow (heat edge). The *_glow emissive maps are greyscale HEAT MASKS for the kiln molten shader (luminance = heat); emissive strength 4.0 / 3.0 in KHR_materials_emissive_strength. Sockets: socket_core (chest core, weak point), socket_head, socket_attack_l/_r (blade tips). Debris: every ceramic plate is a separate loose island rigidly weighted to one bone; vertex attribute _plate (glTF _PLATE, three.js geometry.attributes._plate) holds the plate index listed in 'plates' (indices are regenerated on every model build: always read them from this file). Big plates (good debris) ride on: blade_l, blade_r, clavicle_l, clavicle_r, dorsal_01, dorsal_02, dorsal_03, dorsal_04, dorsal_05, dorsal_06, dorsal_07, dorsal_08, forearm_l, forearm_r, head, pelvis, shin_l, shin_r, thigh_l, thigh_r. Event times per clip: spawn: ignite_start 0.080, claw_hit 0.300, shake 0.800, ignite_full 0.950; idle: flick 1.080, scrape 2.300; run: footstep_l 0.000, footstep_r 0.300; leap: launch 0.330, apex 0.500, land 0.700, impact 0.745; attack_a: telegraph 0.190, impact 0.267; attack_b: telegraph 0.240, impact 0.365; hit: hit 0.000; stagger: stagger 0.000, vulnerable_start 0.100, blade_scrape 0.400, vulnerable_end 0.950; death_a: death 0.100, gutter_start 0.400, ground_hit 0.420, twitch 1.190, gutter_end 1.400; death_b: death 0.000, gutter_start 0.350, ground_hit 0.370, ground_hit 0.530, twitch 1.040, gutter_end 1.220."
